    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n102522" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τατύρας</span></b> , ὁ, oriental
		name of the <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>pheasant</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pamphil.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				9.387e
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέταρος, τέτραξ</span>. (Cf.
			Mod. <i><span class="en">
				Pers.
			</span></i>
			<i>tedzrev</i> 'pheasant', Lith. <i>teterva</i> 'black grouse',
			etc.: the bird <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέταρος</span> was imported
			from Media acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				14.654c
			</span></i>.)</div>
